# This deposit is verified by SHA-256, so git must hand back the same bytes it
# was given on every platform. `-text` disables end-of-line conversion; without
# it a clone on Windows rewrites line endings and every text entry in
# SHA256_MANIFEST.csv fails to verify. Diffs are unaffected: git still detects
# text on its own for that.
#
# The tree is deliberately mixed. Source and documentation are LF; the CSV and
# JSON files are written by pandas and json on Windows and carry CRLF. Both are
# hashed as they are.
* -text
